 "drivingQuestion": "Does the halakha follow R. Yehuda?",
 "outcome": "not_dialectical",
 "outcomeNote": "conflicting rulings recorded without decision",
 "continuesQuestionOf": null,
 "segments": [
  {
   "id": "sanhedrin.28b.25",
   "daf": "28b",
   "sentenceId": 24,
   "he": "רַבִּי יְהוּדָה אוֹמֵר כּוּ׳. אָמַר רַבִּי תַּנְחוּם אָמַר רַבִּי טַבְלָא אָמַר רַבִּי בְּרוֹנָא אָמַר רַב: הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה. רָבָא אָמַר רַב נַחְמָן: אֵין הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה. וְכֵן אָמַר רַבָּה בַּר בַּר חָנָה אָמַר רַבִּי יוֹחָנָן: אֵין הֲלָכָה כְּרַבִּי יְהוּדָה.",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «Rabbi Yehuda says» that if the witness married the daughter of one of the litigants he is disqualified even if the daughter died, provided that he has children from her. «Rabbi Tanḥum says» that «Rabbi Tavla says» that «Rabbi Beruna says» that «Rav says:» The «halakha» is «in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda. Rava» says that «Rav Naḥman says:» The «halakha» is «not in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda. And likewise Rabba bar bar Ḥana says» that «Rabbi Yoḥanan says:» The «halakha» is «not in accordance with» the opinion of «Rabbi Yehuda.»"
  }
 ],
